accessWidener v2 official

# `official` rather than `named`, and there is no longer a difference: Minecraft is unobfuscated from 26.1,
# so there is one namespace and Loom expects it to be called this. It says so plainly if it is not —
# "Expected official namespace for access widener entry, found: named".

# Region-aware surface painting (co.voik.agesandtheart.worldgen.field.RegionRule).
#
# Both of these are declared `protected` INSIDE SurfaceRules, which makes every extension point in the
# surface system unreachable from outside Mojang's package: a custom RuleSource cannot name the type it
# returns, and a custom ConditionSource cannot read the column it is being asked about.
#
# Note that `javap` reports them as public — a nested type's class file carries its own flags, while the
# real nesting modifier lives in the outer class's InnerClasses attribute. Kotlin reads the latter.
#
# We only need to *name* these; no members are touched. RegionRule passes the Context straight through to
# its children and takes its coordinates from tryApply's arguments instead.
#
# RETAINED ON PURPOSE, 2026-07-29: nothing constructs a RegionRule at the moment. Deleting the dressing left a
# composed Age wearing one plain palette, and materials moved into the fill in step 4. Jonah's call is to keep
# both the class and these two lines, because per-territory painting is expected back in the biome pass. If
# that ever stops being true, RegionRule and these two lines go together and only the NoiseBasedChunkGenerator
# line below is load-bearing.
accessible	class	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$Context
accessible	class	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$SurfaceRule

# Writing a condition of our own (co.voik.agesandtheart.worldgen.field.NearTheSurface) — the case the note
# above says the vocabulary is closed to.
#
# `Condition` is the type a ConditionSource returns, and it is package-private, so the public
# `ConditionSource` cannot in fact be implemented from outside Mojang's package. The three fields are the
# position the condition is being asked about; `Context` itself is already named above, but its coordinates
# are package-private too, and a condition that cannot read them can only answer constants.
#
# What it buys: `abovePreliminarySurface` compares against a heightmap sampled at the corners of a 16-block
# cell and **bilinearly interpolated** across it, which is sound for vanilla's terrain and wrong for ours —
# a gorge floor narrower than the cell reads as far underground and loses its skin, and a cave under a
# steep slope reads as open ground and grows grass. Ours asks the field for the column it is standing in.
accessible	class	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$Condition
accessible	field	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$Context	blockX	I
accessible	field	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$Context	blockY	I
accessible	field	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$Context	blockZ	I

# So AgeChunkGenerator can BE a noise generator rather than sit beside one.
#
# The class is `final`; every method we override is already public and non-final, so this one line is the
# whole toll. What it buys is the `instanceof NoiseBasedChunkGenerator` branch in `ChunkMap`, which decides
# whether the game builds our RandomState from our own settings or from `NoiseGeneratorSettings.dummy()`.
# A peer can never be handed a real climate sampler; a subclass is.
#
# Well-trodden ground rather than a novel liberty: Botania, Bumblezone, Twilight Forest and moderner-beta
# all ship this exact line. (Botania's NeoForge half is `public-f` on the same class, as ours is.)
#
# Beware: the decompiled sources DROP the `final` from the class declaration. Only `javap` and the compiler
# tell the truth about modifiers here.
extendable	class	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/NoiseBasedChunkGenerator

# So a BlockEntityType can be built in `common` (co.voik.agesandtheart.content.AgeContent).
#
# 26.1 made the constructor private and deleted `BlockEntityType.Builder`, leaving vanilla's own
# construct-and-register-in-one-expression as the only sanctioned route. Each loader offers a substitute —
# Fabric's `FabricBlockEntityTypeBuilder`, NeoForge's registry helpers — but taking those would push
# construction into both loader modules and need a service to hand the type back to common, which is a lot
# of machinery to avoid one line.
#
# Safe because registration still happens during mod init, before the registry freezes: the intrusive
# holder the constructor creates is bound by `Registry.register` exactly as vanilla's is.
accessible	method	net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType	<init>	(Lnet/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType$BlockEntitySupplier;Ljava/util/Set;)V

# So a MenuType can be built in `common`, for the same reason as BlockEntityType above — 26.1 keeps the
# constructor private and offers only vanilla's private `register`.
accessible	method	net/minecraft/world/inventory/MenuType	<init>	(Lnet/minecraft/world/inventory/MenuType$MenuSupplier;Lnet/minecraft/world/flag/FeatureFlagSet;)V

# So an Age can decide its own features (co.voik.agesandtheart.age.aspect.Features).
#
# `generationSettingsGetter` is how vanilla itself parameterises this: `ChunkGenerator`'s two-argument
# constructor takes the function, and both readers of features go through it — the memoised
# `featuresPerStep`, and `applyBiomeDecoration`'s own lookup. It is the sanctioned seam and we cannot reach
# it, because `NoiseBasedChunkGenerator` calls `super(biomeSource)` and never offers the second argument.
#
# So the field is made writable and assigned once, immediately after construction — and **so is
# `featuresPerStep`, because vanilla's constructor captures the *parameter* rather than the field**:
#
#     this.generationSettingsGetter = generationSettingsGetter;
#     this.featuresPerStep = Suppliers.memoize(() -> buildFeaturesPerStep(..., generationSettingsGetter, ...));
#
# Writing only the field moves `applyBiomeDecoration`'s lookup and leaves the sorted list it indexes into
# built from the biome defaults, so a feature the Age added is looked up in a list that never had it. The
# index is identity-based (`Util.createIndexIdentityLookup`) and misses as -1, which is an
# `IndexOutOfBoundsException` in the middle of decoration. The two fields have to move together.
#
# The alternative was overriding `applyBiomeDecoration` outright: sixty lines of vanilla's own structure
# and feature placement copied to change one lookup, and `featuresPerStep` is private, so the sorted list
# would have to be rebuilt beside it.
accessible	field	net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkGenerator	generationSettingsGetter	Ljava/util/function/Function;
mutable	field	net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkGenerator	generationSettingsGetter	Ljava/util/function/Function;
accessible	field	net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkGenerator	featuresPerStep	Ljava/util/function/Supplier;
mutable	field	net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/ChunkGenerator	featuresPerStep	Ljava/util/function/Supplier;

# So a bolt we call down can be aimed the way vanilla aims one (co.voik.agesandtheart.age.phenomena.Tempest).
#
# **The lightning rod is found by the spawner, not by the bolt**, and that is the whole reason this line
# exists. `tickThunder` calls `findLightningTargetAround` *before* anything is created, so the strike is
# moved onto a rod within 128 blocks while it is still only a position — a bolt built at a coordinate and
# added to the world has already declined the redirect, and no amount of copper will save what is under it.
#
# There is no public equivalent. `tickThunder` itself is public but gated on rain, thunder and a 1 in
# 100,000 roll, so it cannot answer "strike *here*"; and reimplementing the search means copying vanilla's
# POI query and its surface test, which is exactly the pair that would drift.
accessible	method	net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel	findLightningTargetAround	(Lnet/minecraft/core/BlockPos;)Lnet/minecraft/core/BlockPos;

# So an Age wearing vanilla's rock can still ask whether the sky is open
# (co.voik.agesandtheart.worldgen.AgeChunkGenerator.skyIsOpenAt).
#
# The gate exists for the creatures vanilla never spawns and so wrote no placement rule for — a dragon, a
# wither, the golems — which `NO_RESTRICTIONS` would otherwise put inside a mountain. An Age with a field of
# ours asks the field; one wearing the template's rock has none, and answering "yes, always" made the gate
# inert for every book that never named a landform.
#
# `getMobsAt` is handed a `StructureManager` and nothing else that knows the world, and the level it holds
# is private with no accessor. It is a plain read of a heightmap vanilla itself keeps for the purpose.
accessible	field	net/minecraft/world/level/StructureManager	level	Lnet/minecraft/world/level/LevelAccessor;

# So a world's own skin can be laid over a rock a book named, rather than instead of it
# (co.voik.agesandtheart.worldgen.field.SurfacingStrategy.asPatchesOver).
#
# A surface tree is supposed to paint patches and leave the bulk to `defaultBlock`, which is what makes
# substituting that block the way a book changes what a world is made of. Two of vanilla's three break it:
# `SurfaceRuleData.nether()` ends in a bare `NETHERRACK` arm that takes every block its conditioned arms
# did not, and `end()` is one unconditional `ENDSTONE` and nothing else. So a blackstone nether came out
# netherrack (Jonah, 2026-08-25, walked).
#
# **Removing that tail is a no-op until the rock is substituted**, which is why it is safe to do always:
# `SurfaceSystem.buildSurface` consults the rule only where `old == this.defaultBlock` and leaves the block
# alone when the rule declines, so an arm painting netherrack onto netherrack is already doing nothing.
#
# We only need to *name* these two, to take a sequence apart and to recognise the unconditional arm at the
# end of it. No members are touched — a record's own accessors are public. The alternatives were rebuilding
# vanilla's ninety-line nether tree by hand, which would drift on every update, and taking the tree apart
# through its codec as JSON, which is string-typed and would fail silently on a shape change.
accessible	class	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$SequenceRuleSource
accessible	class	net/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/SurfaceRules$BlockRuleSource

# So a render type of ours can carry a pipeline of ours (co.voik.agesandtheart.client.SandColumnRenderer).
#
# **`RenderSetup.builder(RenderPipeline)` is public and this is the only thing that is not**, which is why
# the shader route costs one line rather than the machinery it looked like it would. A `RenderPipeline`
# needs no registration at all — Blaze3D compiles one on first use through `ShaderManager`, which scans
# `shaders/` across every namespace — but a pipeline can only reach the retained-mode renderer as a
# `RenderType`, and `RenderType.create` is package-private.
#
# What it buys is the sandfall's roil running per *fragment* (design §5.2.2). The alternative was evaluating
# it per vertex on the CPU, which is tens of thousands of vertices rebuilt every frame against this route's
# handful of quads, for the coarse interpolated wash Ephemeris already moved off.
accessible	method	net/minecraft/client/renderer/rendertype/RenderType	create	(Ljava/lang/String;Lnet/minecraft/client/renderer/rendertype/RenderSetup;)Lnet/minecraft/client/renderer/rendertype/RenderType;

# So the linking panel's orbit camera can have a frustum and a projection
# (co.voik.agesandtheart.client.panel.PanelCamera, design §7.8.1).
#
# `setPosition` and `setRotation` are already `protected`, so a subclass places the camera without help.
# **These two are private**, and the only public path that calls them — `Camera.update(DeltaTracker)` —
# aligns the camera to `minecraft.player` and would throw the orbit away. A camera whose `getCullFrustum()`
# is meaningless renders nothing, and that is exactly what `LevelRenderer.extractLevel` asks for.
#
# The alternative was assembling a `CameraRenderState` by hand and never using `Camera` at all. Declined:
# it means reimplementing vanilla's culling maths, and disagreeing with it shows up as chunks silently
# missing from the panel rather than as anything that fails.
accessible	method	net/minecraft/client/Camera	prepareCullFrustum	(Lorg/joml/Matrix4fc;Lorg/joml/Matrix4f;Lnet/minecraft/world/phys/Vec3;)V
accessible	method	net/minecraft/client/Camera	setupPerspective	(FFFFF)V
